To tell you the truth, I just went to the oss site at www.4front-tech.com
and pulled down the shareware drivers. You have to get the binaries specific
to your machine and kernel, but after that it was pretty much a snap. Make
sure that you tell it to use the Digital Built-In Audio, or something that
sounds like that, anyway, and that the settings are io=530, IRQ=9 and DMA=3
(The default DMA that it wants to use is 0 or 1, but they obviously won't
work in this configuration).

HTH
JA
