>You still don't seem to understand the point.

I asked a question, I didn't make a statement.  I'm trying to help our
management gather information that will help them make a decision.  Most of
the people who have written to us name the software licensing fees for
DIGITAL UNIX as the major reason they are using Linux.  *I* know that that's
not the only reason one uses Linux, but we need to hear it from users.

As far as any "petition" goes - we haven't seen any formal collection of
requests.

Compaq would very much like to encourage use of Alpha systems, and Compaq's
upper management thinks Linux is a good way to broaden the Alpha market.  No
argument from me on that!  We have come up with estimates on what it would
cost us to offer a F90 product on Alpha Linux, and presented them to
management.  What would influence them in favor of the proposal is to know
that there are a large number of customers who would pay a reasonable price
($500 is the figure most users I've corresponded with have centered on) for
a compiler, and that the support costs wouldn't eat us alive.  (We are
concerned about the idea that everyone's Linux system is different from
everyone else's...)

If you have comments you'd like me to pass on to our management, just send
them to me by e-mail.

