> sources?

I don't expect anything, I'm just answering your question.


> The other commerical vendors offering Linux products
> don't seem to be supplying sources either.

Depends.  For instance Corel has some binary-only products and some
that come with source.  I have only bought the latter.

I would consider a binary-only product if, in decreasing order of importance:

  1. It scratches a big itch.
  2. It comes with a liberal license.
  3. I trust the vendor to fix any bugs discovered, quickly.
  4. The price is right.

Software with source usually fits 2 & 3.  I would be willing to pay
twice as much for the same product with source as without.

Rob.



