I recently had my Multia flake out on me.  I had telneted into it before
to work and it was fine, we had a power outtage while I was away and
when I came home I noticed the link light on the hub was blinking (3
sec's on, 2 sec's off repititiously).
I tried to telnet into it again, but no luck, couldnt ping it either.
So i turned on it's monitor and logged in.  Everthing went fine except I
couldnt telnet or ping out.  Definitely something wrong with my built in
NIC I thought.  So, I figure I'd swap Cat 5 cables, since this had
actually fixed some problems I had before.  Viola!  The link light
stayed solid and I was able to ping and telnet freely.  The cable that
was on there I hooked to my Win95 PC and it worked like a champ as
well.  I had previously tried re-inserting the RJ45 plug into the socket
on the multia with no change.  This time, when I plugged in the other
cable it came up on the screen saying something like "eth0 is type TP"
or some such. Anyway, this is really weird.  Especially since it was
working only a few hours before and the cable that was in there is
working fine on my PC as I type.

What's my point?  Um, I dont have one.  But if you have ethernet
connectivity problems, try swapping Cat 5 cables.

-Ken





