In article <3686c0f9.29945684@news.uunet.be>, Tom Rogie wrote:
>arch/alpha/Makefile:30: *** missing separator.  Stop.

The behaviour of
$(shell foobar)
changed in recent versions of GNU make.  Either change to a different
version of make, or edit the Makefile so it says
x=$(shell foobar)
instead.

The change is that in old versions of make,
$(shell foobar)
evaluated to "" (nothing).  The more recent versions of make evaluate
that to "1" or "0" depending on the exit value of the shell command,
and that number is a syntax error in make.

I don't know if they may have changed the behaviour back in the most
recent version.

-andy



