Erik-Jan Sinke wrote:
> 
> Hi there,
> 
> I�m trying to set up my Alpha Linux box to recognize both of my ethernet
> adapters. I know that under "Intel" Linux you have to add an
> append="ether,IRQ,Address,eth1" statement to the lilo.conf. How does this
> work with MILO? Does it also have a MILO.conf and if so where should I put
> it?
> I�m booting with the help of the NT ARC console and have put the following
> line in the OSLOADOPTIONS :
> boot sda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2
> 
> Thanx in advance,
> Erik

On my alpha also booted by MILO via NT ARC console I put in the
OSLOADOPTIONS the following line:

boot sda2:vmlinux.gz ether=0,0,eth1 root=/dev/sda2

and it works.

The two zeros stand for autoprobing the IRQ and ADDRESS. It should work
on your machine too.


Good luck

Renato Tognaccini
University of Naples



