G. Hugh SONG <ghsong@\"Spamspoiler\"kjist.ac.kr> wrote in message
news:76c3qc$e3c$1@news.kjist.ac.kr...

>Although we have our representative in that non-monolithic land,
>we still have not heard any Christmas news from Digipaq.
>The recent note written to this newsgroup was that a business
>case of F90 for Linux/Alpha was being reviewed within Digipaq.
>
>Could Steve or Jon tell us what is going on within Digipaq?
>Of course, I need to know as soon as possible since I need to decide
>which to buy, P2 or more 21164.

The issues are still under review.  However, I want to point out that it's
not merely a case of saying "yes" and magically, a compiler appears next
week.  An Alpha Linux port of our compiler would require significant new
engineering work due to the different linking, debugging and OS feature
environment of Linux.  Just for starters, Alpha Linux uses ELF for its
object language, while DIGITAL UNIX uses COFF.  We don't currently generate
ELF on any of our platforms.  Even if a decision was made today to go ahead,
you wouldn't see anything before next Christmas at the very earliest.

