>Hello,
>
>
>I finally succeeded in compiling a new kernel. But when I boot the new
>kernel on my UDB, the screen suddenly stops with the (last) message:
>
>...turnign on virtual addressing and jumping to the Linux Kernel
>
>then the machine continues to boot but the screen doesn't change
>anymore. I can telnet to the UDB but I get no login on the console.
>Did I forget to compile something important into the kernel? I just
>can't figger out what...

You've got the wrong console options turned on.  Make sure that only
one of TGA and VGA is configured into the kernel, and that you've
selected the appropriate options with regards to where the console
goes.

Also be sure to use `make config' rather than menuconfig or xconfig,
as the latter two may not be completely up to date.

-andy



