You still don't seem to understand the point.
Those of us, who use computers for living, spend almost equal time
administrating it as well as using the applications.  Unfortunately,
that sort of statement is true even for my MS Windows PC (due to flakyness
of M$ Windows).   And most of us are not system administrators although
we know those stuff more than those SA's we hire.

Unfortunately, adminitrative things are all different among
different flavors of Unices-- Solaris, HPUX, DU(Ultrix), Linux, you
name it.  And I really don't want to spend any more time for
administrative burdens.

