Joachim Wesner wrote:

> Bram wrote:

> > I've been reading DEC's Assembly Language Programmer's Guide.
> > But I have a couple of questions.

> > How can I have egcs generate more verbose assembly output?
> > The samples in the guide show the C-source as comments in
> > the assembly file.
> > The output from egcc -S does not give these.

> To my knowledge, there is no way to have the assembly output mixed with
> the C-source on gcc/egcs.

Well, I never got around writing this, but the egcc -g -S [other
options] ... command should write the debugging information in the
assembler file, and hence - because the debugging info contains the line
number - it's possible (writing a small C program that reads both the .s
and the .c file) to create a combined file with the assembler code
interspersed with the original C code.

