Erik-Jan Sinke <Zijlware111@multiweb.nl> wrote:
: Hi there,
Hello!

: My AXPPCI33 Alpha system is suffering from the following problem :
: I boot up the machine with the help of MILO (Standard RedHAT 5.2 MILO).
: However, when MILO has finished loading and I try to type anything at the
: prompt my keyboard keys are all mixed up. I have recently updated the flash
: to the latest level and think I�ve configured my keyboard the right way in
: the System setup (US Keyboard). (Running the same machine under NT does not
: generate any keyboard problems).
: Does anybody out there have a solution for this problem?
Do you have _anything_ connected to your first serial port?
A mouse? A modem? Something else that is active on bootup (i.e. switched
on)?
If yes: Plug it off, turn it off or remove it any other way!
Milo sends status reports to the first serial port by default and also
accepts commands from there. That's the most probable fault...

