Timothy K Canfield <tkc+@andrew.cmu.edu> wrote:
> configuring the network using DHCP i recieve unaligned trap.  This also

I don't know about redhat, but if it uses - like debian - dhcpcd 0.70,
then these unaligned traps are caused by long-pointer-casts:

u_long foo;
u_char *bar;
...
foo= *((u_long *) bar);

If the char-pointer is not 64-bit aligned, this gives an unaligned 
access violation.  I replaced these instructions by

memcpy(&foo,bar,sizeof(long));

to get rid of the unaligned accesses.  But this is ofcourse not an optimal
way of solving the problem.  Aren't there any macros definedto do this 
type of unaligned long copying?

Tom



















