I don't know how big you mean... if they are at least a few dozen
digits, then you could take a look at GMP:

  http://www.matematik.su.se/~tege/gmp/


It contains optimised low-level arithmetic routines for several chips
which make interesting reading.  Its author, Torbjo"rn Granlund,
appears to agree about the speed of Alpha.  See the speed charts at:

  http://www.matematik.su.se/~tege/gmp/gmp-speed.html


Typically, mpn_addmul is the critical function.  Torbjo"rn's code for
it was 5 times faster on a 500 MHz Alpha than a 200 MHz Pentium Pro.
This was measured a while ago so a more up-to-date comparison would be
something like a factor of three between a 600 MHz Alpha and a 400 MHz P II.
I'm just waiting to see his numbers on 21264 chips!

Rob.



