Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

I am using DU just because of the FORTRAN.  This is because I
have a production application (very large code written in FORTRAN) 
that runs significantly faster under DU/f77 than Linux/g77.

Furthermore, because this large legacy code also contains several
places that generate floating point errors (divide by zero, overflow,
etc.), DU/f77 is required to acieve the "correct" results.  Otherwise,
under LInux/g77 the code would die.

So, until the floating point performance of g77 is as good as f77, and
until the floating point error processing under g77 is as good as f77
(see fpe1, fpe2, etc. f77 options), I will be forced to use DU.

This is a shame because all other aspects of Linux for the Alpha are
in good shape as far as I am concerned.  I still use Linux on my Intel
machines 100% of the time.

