If the AXPpci33 card has the SRM console it is probably configured for serial
console mode.  The best thing you can do is hook up a terminal device of sort 
to the com port and see if you are getting anything there when you boot up.  
If this turns out to be the case, issue the command "set console graphic" at 
the >>> SRM prompt and reboot.

If you have a board with the ARC console or if the SRM console is already set 
to graphics mode, you must have a keyboard and graphics card installed.  If a 
keyboard is not found, the system will default to serial mode...

A third and more distant possibility is that someone has configured the boot 
jumpers on the board for a fail safe boot.  I mention this possibility because 
unlike Intel,  Alpha systems do not normally attempt a floppy boot on startup.

Bob Segrest


