Hi:

I'm trying to follow the instructions in the Redhat manuals to install
RedHat v5.2 on this LX164 box.  I made a FAT floppy and copied
Linload.exe onto it.  Then I copied the /MILO/LX164 image to the floppy
and renamed it Milo.  I did this from a windows 95 machine.  I made a
boot entry in the AlphaBios telling it to run linload.exe from device a:
and directory \

When I try to boot from it, I get Invalid Operating System Selection. 
I've got AlphaBios 5.62-1a on the machine.  The instructions say use the
latest Bios, but I can't find one for my machine.  The URL in RedHat's
manual is not current.

Also, I saw a message about not being able to boot from disks not made
on an Alpha, but mine (running RedHat 5.0, kernel 2.0.35-2) thinks the
floppy is 2.88 MB, and can't read or write normal floppies that other
machines can read.  Maybe that's my problem?
