Not AFAIK. You need a kernel compiled with a serial console option. I 
just put a graphic-card in mine for installation, because even if you
get the kernel to boot on the serial I don't think the redhat-install will
work there. It uses 4 or 5 virtual consoles, you only need the first, but I
think it won't work anyway. After installation you can remove the card again.
You only need some luck in selecting the right one, the card must be able
to initialize itsef without help of the CPU to work with the SRM console. 
I tried quite a few old VGA cards to find a suitable one. Or just find
an ELSA Winner 1000 Twinbus (ISA only should do, too), that one is known
to work.

