Hello,

I have an AlphaServer 1000A 5/400 running NT server 4.0. I would like to upgrade
it to Linux. This machine includes: 

- Network card: 	DecChip 21140
- SCSI controllers: 	- Mylex DAC960/Digital SWXCR-Ex (the disks)
			- QLogic PCI SCSI Host Adapter (CD-ROM and tape)
- CDROM: 		DEC RRD45
- Tape: 		DEC TLZ7
- Display: 		ati compatible display adapter
- 4 disks 2.1 GB
- 256MB RAM

(All the above as presented from WinNT).

I had a look in all related FAQs, including the Mylex Linux driver page. But i
still have some questions: 

- I haven't seen any specific reference to this system. Is it possible to
install Linux ? If yes, how easy it is ? I did'nt even managed to find out the
exact model of the motherboard. Is there a straightforward installing procedure
? If i have the RedHat Alpha Linux package, i will need extra software and/or
strange procedures to make the installation ?

- Concerning the Mylex controller, (which controls the disk drives), the
driver's page mentions specific models (of the driver) that are supported. How
can i determine the controller's model without rebooting and/or just opening the
case ?

- How long do you think that the downtime will be if everything goes ok ? Anyone
with installation and operation experience on the specific model ?

Thanks in advance,

Theodore

