Hi,

I'm considering a 533MHz Alpha system based on either the older LX board
or the newer UX2 (Ruffian) board.  The machine will be used mostly for
C/C++ development, so stability is paramount.  I'm leaning towards the
UX because the SCSI and Enet controllers are integrated thus leaving
more slots free but if Linux is less stable than on the LX board, I'll
go with the older board.

I'd very much appreciate comments from people who are running RH5.2 on
these systems. Specifically:

1. Is RH5.2 stable on either (or both) these boards ? I've heard
   conflicting things about the UX board: Some people claim Linux (or
   at least the RH5.2 distribution) is unstable. The Apache guys (see
   http://www.apache.com) have actually removed the Alpha from their
   list of standard systems while they try to resolve the problems.
   Other vendors (e.g. DCG, http://www.dcginc.com) claim it runs fine.
   Yet others (e.g. harddata) claim extensive modifications are needed
   Can anybody shed some light here ?

2. How good are the Linux drivers for the built-in Symbios SCSI and Enet
   controllers on the UX board ?

3. Some vendors claim that putting a slow SCSI device (e.g. CDROM) on
   the same chain as the hard disk will slow everything down from
   40MB/s to the 10MB/s speed of the slow device and are therefore
   recommending an IDE CDROM instead; one vendor has actually
   recommended getting a _second_ SCSI controller just for the CDROM.
   Others claim there is no problem at all with having both fast and
   slow devices on the same chain.  Does anyone know what the real
   story is here ?

Thanks for any info.

Ram



