I'm running Red Hat 5.1 on my LX164. What I have done to have a correct
RTC is:

1. Edit the file /etc/sysconfig/clock to look like
        UTC=true
        ARC=true

2. To set the RTC to system time execute clock -usA.

If you are running Red Hat, item 1 will fix you up on subsequent reboots.

