Hi!

There were quite a lot of requests for help with installation of
Redhat 5.2 on UX-based systems. I did such an installation recently,
so maybe the images of the working boot disks will help someone
here. They are available via WWW at

http://www.theophys.kth.se/~jurijus/alpha
SEE DISCLAIMER BELOW!

There are four images available:

milo.img   : contains milo and ldmilo.exe (1st in sequence)
kernel.img : contains image of the kernel (2nd in sequence)
ramdisk.img: contains image of the ramdisk (3rd in sequence)
arcinst.img: contains arcinst.exe (needed to format the small boot
             partition for DOS)

Note: there is an unconfirmed information, that for successful
installation you have to create the floppies on a Alpha machine.
Disks created on PC or other machines may not always work.
I have an indirect evidence for that :))

The outline of installation on a system with a single SCSI
hard drive is as follows:
1. Turn on computer, wait for devices detection.
2. Insert milo disk and choose Run Command from ARCBIOS menu.
   Type the name of the command: "a:ldmilo.exe". The milo
   image should load and dump you to the MILO prompt.
3. Insert kernel disk and at the milo prompt type "boot floppy".
4. After some time the system will prompt you for ramdisk.
   Insert it, press ENTER.
5. This should bring you to the Redhat installation screen. Create
   the following disk partitions:
   a) Primary, with size 4MB and type "DOS >= 32MB", /dev/sda1
   b) Extended, over the rest of the disk, /dev/sda2
   c) Logical, with size 1-3 times RAM and type "Linux Swap", /dev/sda5
   d) Logical, over the rest of /dev/sda2 and type "Linux Native", /dev/sda6
6. Install Redhat. After the installation ends it will prompt you to
   insert the kernel disk to copy the kernel. Wait till reboot.
7. After everything stops, make a cold reboot.
8. Insert arcinst disk, choose "Run Command" -> "a:arcinst.exe" from
   ARCBIOS menu.
9. Use arcinst to format you small 4MB partition as DOS. After you are
   done, return to ARCBIOS.
10. Make a cold reboot.
11. Load MILO from floppy as before.
12. At the MILO prompt type: "boot sda6:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda6". The Redhat
   should load from the hard disk now.
13. Login as root.
14. Insert MILO floppy.
15. Mount floppy: "mount -t msdos /dev/fd0 /mnt/floppy"
16. Mount /dev/sda1: "mount -t msdos /dev/sda1 /msdos"
17. Copy all files from floppy to partition:
    "cp /mnt/floppy/* /msdos/"
18. Unmount everything.
19. Shutdown and make a cold reboot.
20. Create Environment Variable Set with System Partition ->
    "FAT File System" and type "Windows NT Workstation 4.00"
    Edit Environment variable set to contain something like
    LoadIdentifier = Linux
    OsLoader = scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)ldmilo.exe
    OsLoadFileName=\
    OsLoadOptions = boot sda6:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda6
    Return to boot options menu.
21. Reboot and load Linux from your hard disk.

DISCLAIMER:
I CANNOT BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ANY DAMAGE, CAUSED BY THIS
PROCEDURE OR DISK IMAGES. EVERYTHING YOU DO, YOU DO ON YOUR OWN
RISK. YOU'D BETTER KNOW, WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

Have fun and good luck.

Regards,

Jurij.

