Robert Harley wrote:

> manoweb@iname.com (Alessio Sangalli) writes:
> > what's th l3 cache speed on modern alpha boxes???
>
> For a while the LX and UX boards had 2 MB of 9 ns SRAMs and the SX
> boards had 1 MB of 7.5 ns (AFAIK).
>
> I just heard yesterday from a vendor that the UX boards now have
> either 2 MB of 8 ns or 4 MB of 7 ns on them.
>
> I vaguely recall reading a while ago that some high-end machines from
> Digital had 6 ns L3...
>

This is a function of availability of SRAM speed as opposed to performance
of the cache.   8 Mbit SRAMs tend to come out in faster speed grades.

If one were to look at SROM source where the cache speed is set, there
is a statement for standard access time if I recall correctly of 8.5 nsec.






