>Quick question... how big is the working set of the program in

I sized the problem it was working on (data) at about 20M, which is
larger than the cache on any machine I know of.

The working set of the program I expect would easily fit into a 1M cache,
possibly a 512M or 256M cache.

>question?  If the working set fits in the caches of EV56 and it is
>mostly FPU issue bound then there wouldn't be a big boost in
>performance for EV6.  Any ideas?

Your explanation is entirely possible.  But I get only 80MFlops (I think) or so
from the code on a 600MHz 21164.  I was hoping that the smarter architecture
could get more out of the FPU.

I might be better off with a simpler CPU which has more FP execution units....

Anyway, for my code, Alpha is still the fastest game in town.....

PeterM



