Andrew F. Seila (andy@ludwig.cba.uga.edu) wrote:
: I would also like to run Modula-3 on an Alpha XL300 running RedHat Linux
: 5.1.  I would be willing to try to compile it if someone who has experience
: porting Modula-3 is willing to help out.

:  Last February, I was in touch with Dragisa Duric <dragisha@rstel.net>, who
: indicated that he was in the process of porting Modula-3 to Linux/Alpha.
: However, I have not been able to contact him recently.  I don't know what
: the situation is - maybe a change of priorities.

: I would guess that the primary problem in porting to Linux/Alpha is 64-bit
: addressing.

  Last February I finished most of port for RedHat 4.2 Linux/Alpha. Only
problem I have with this port is multithreading - something I had not idea
how to solve at moment. Other tasks took my time from February to November.

  Most of applications does work - including cvsup (with @M3nopreemption).
Compiler does not have visible problems.

  Last month I installed RedHat 5.0 on my Alpha and porting is now little
more difficult due to libc6 problems. My Alpha is also headless. This slows
me down as I need to make bootstrap frequently. My Intel boxes are both pm3
and I am making bootstrap archive on RedHat 4.2 on Alpha :). Yes - I am
porting on SRC M3 3.6 but I don't think there will be any problems once I
finish it to move to pm3.

  64-bit addressing was not problem except in C dependent parts
(m3core/src/unix/...) as libc heads are only recently aware of
sizeof(int)<>sizeof(long) and sizeof(int)<>sizeof(address). Lots of *.h
constants are changed to be compatible with Digital UNIX due to project
decisions made by Linus Torvalds and this was another problem.

  dd



