It has to do with the way that Alpha access memory(If I remember
correctly).

It's not a problem with Linux itself, but rather the application
you are running (X). The kernel is trapping this access and
in a sense fixing it for you then letting it go in. The message
is just a warning. The only problem is that you take a small
performance hit. I can provide a more technical answer if you'd
like as I have some info on the written down, just not with me!!

