I have certainly seen a range of performance improvements
going to an EV6 from an EV5.  Some of our larger codes
do get the 2x improvement after recompiling with the appropriate
switches.  As with any cache-based system, your milage will
vary.

One of my little codes doesnt improve at all on an EV6. But it
is also exactly what I expected since the code is quite cache
friendly and lets the CPU issue and retire 2 floating point
instructions on every clock cycle.  Since the EV6 FP unit
is very similar to EV5, this is the expected result.  This code
will scale with the CPU clock.





