In article <3665C108.C562151@rhea.umd.edu>,
Jeffrey J. Potoff <jpotoff@rhea.umd.edu> wrote:

>Any ideas for why the performance is quite a bit below the
>expected "2-3x" improvement we've been hearing about ?
>I'm becoming somewhat concerned since we were planning 
>on buying a number of machines based on this chip/board.

Performance on any single benchmark is NOT a fair test
of overall performance!  *I* got modest improvement, *you* may
get a 4x improvement!

The SPECfp95 suite of codes gets a 2-3x improvement with a 21264,
and that's a MUCH fairer test than my one program.

Don't get too scared by this test.  MY particular code, compiled
with a possibly non-optimal compiler for the 21264 (DEC CXX 6.0),
didn't get the 2x performance.

I'm not ready to give up yet, though.  If I can get access to a 21264 box,
I'll try out new compilers and different flags.

Anyway, what I recommend you do is test your own application on
a 21264.  I got a 19% speedup, YOU may get a 4x speedup.

Peter Mardahl



