How did you -tune the program when you compiled it?   Also, what
was the -arch specifier.  They are different.

Basically -tune tunes the base instruction set for the issue properties
of the architecture, -arch allows the use of any additional instructions
also but may cause the code to take an emulation hit on older
architecture machines.

Bill Parke

